# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and in the working copy,
# whatever platform a file was written on. Without this a file edited on
# Windows and the same file edited on Linux differ in every line, which buries
# the change that was actually made and makes a merge conflict of a whole file.
# Python reads either ending on either platform, and every editor in use here
# reads LF, so LF is the one that costs nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf
